doc:Factsarticle1_87 dcterms:abstract "Taking the main steam drain valve of a thermal power plant as the research object, and using Mean Absolute Error (MAE), Root-Mean-Squared Error (RMSE), Mean Absolute Percentage Error (MAPE), and symmetric Mean Absolute Percentage Error (sMAPE) as evaluation metrics, a case study on trend prediction of drain valve internal leakage was conducted, comparing the proposed method with ARIMA, Long Short-Term Memory networks (LSTM) and eXtreme Gradient Boosting (XGBoost) methods." .
_:c2c5c7523e4d69adba303d92e6e3ec87 rdf:reifies <<( doc:Factsarticle1_87 dcterms:abstract "Taking the main steam drain valve of a thermal power plant as the research object, and using Mean Absolute Error (MAE), Root-Mean-Squared Error (RMSE), Mean Absolute Percentage Error (MAPE), and symmetric Mean Absolute Percentage Error (sMAPE) as evaluation metrics, a case study on trend prediction of drain valve internal leakage was conducted, comparing the proposed method with ARIMA, Long Short-Term Memory networks (LSTM) and eXtreme Gradient Boosting (XGBoost) methods." )>> ;
